// expect: 3
// The Mycroft fragment (§11 5.3): UNSIG'D polymorphic recursion,
// INFERRED — no annotation anywhere. Round 1 refuses with the poly
// fingerprint, round 2 judges under the general assumption, round 3
// rechecks under the result scheme (the stability round), and the
// published scheme is ∀a. (a, Int) -> Int. Inference where Haskell
// and OCaml demand the annotation. Born as the flip of the teach
// fixture the day the fragment landed.
fn depth(x, n) = if n <= 0 { 0 } else { 1 + depth([x], n - 1) }

fn main() = depth(7, 3)
